BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:CPhaDwrMwupBFdwCMdbV@ccom-dashboard
SUMMARY:ABTA Fall Volunteer Opportunity for Midwestern University Students
LOCATION:Chicago Marathon - Mile 15 (Adams Street and Loomis Street\, West Loop) Parking in lot (Monroe St and Laflin St)\, 555 31st Street\, Downers Grove\, IL 60515\, United States
DESCRIPTION:Join Precision Medicine Club on October 11th at the American Brain Tumor Association Cheer Tent at the Chicago Marathon. Be part of a stellar cheer squad for Team ABTA on Marathon Day! Team ABTA is made up of dedicated individuals who are running to raise funds for brain tumor research and patient programs. As a volunteer you will help set up the ABTA tent and feather banners\, make cheer signs\, greet runners' families\, track and cheer on Team ABTA runners as they pass by\, take photos and enjoy hot coffee and donuts. Wear casual attire and comfortable shoes.\n\nWe need volunteers to help at our ABTA Cheer Tent at the Chicago Marathon on Sunday\, October 11.\nThere are 2 shifts available.  Details are below.\nChicago Marathon Charity Block Party\n \nSun\, October 11 at 6 AM - 11 AM (5 hours)\nSun\, October 11 at 9:30 AM - 2:30 PM (5 hours)\n\nRegister on VolunteerHub: https://abta.volunteerhub.com/vv2/   \n---\nEvent Details: https://mwustudentlife.midwestern.edu/rsvp?id=377590
DTSTART:20261011T110000Z
DTEND:20261011T193000Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6wdo1uY9JsjXiyRgLtrm@ccom-dashboard
SUMMARY:Writing Letters to Trans Folks
LOCATION:Sign in to download the location
DESCRIPTION:Join Pride Club in writing letters to trans youth through Point of Pride! According to the Trevor Project\, trans youth are four times as likely to attempt suicide as their peers. Help us send them support! Letters will be distributed by Point of Pride in care packages to trans youth experiencing barriers to accessing healthcare. Write letters\, have lunch\, and earn TOUCH hours - RSVP by 10/9 for lunch!\n---\nEvent Details: https://mwustudentlife.midwestern.edu/rsvp?id=377443
DTSTART:20261015T170000Z
DTEND:20261015T180000Z
END:VEVENT
